From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:00:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SetupWizard: leave the navigation mode to the platform

The wizard switched a device without an app-switch key to gestural
navigation as soon as it started, before its first page, and its
navigation page then let the person change it back. A product that
hides that page has no choice to ask for, and the forced mode is the
wizard's own, not the platform's. Remove the call and the function that
did it: the device keeps the mode its framework configuration and
overlays give it.

The Finish page explains how to go home for the mode the navigation
page chose and, when no page chose, assumed gestures. It now reads
Settings.Secure.NAVIGATION_MODE when no page chose. The navigation page
itself is unchanged, and a script that lists it behaves as before.
